# Every file is checked out byte for byte, on Windows too (T-109): git for Windows converts LF
# to CRLF by default (core.autocrlf), which breaks the byte-exact fixtures, captures and text
# comparisons the tests make.
* -text
# Source files are text with LF endings everywhere, so an editor set to CRLF cannot commit
# CRLF source.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
